    "_note": "ngram_sizes is [1] deliberately. Backfilled over 30 real episodes, every multi-word phrase that cleared the thresholds was either basic English (\"it's a\", \"rather than\") or subject matter (\"fire season\", \"the region\") — banning those in the prompt would damage the script, and not one real tic surfaced. The adverb class surfaced four (exactly, genuinely, directly, quietly). Division of labour: the ledger machine-detects the adverb register; multi-word tics are what a human notices, and hard_banned is the channel for naming them."
